Prompt: FPS 5v5 3 lane map
Plan: A competitive first-person shooter multiplayer arena built for symmetric 5-versus-5 team combat, laid out as a classic three-lane map where two opposing fortified spawn bases sit at opposite ends of the playspace and are connected by three roughly parallel routes running between them. The setting is a contested industrial site: a decommissioned coastal extraction and refining complex that two rival factions are fighting to control, giving the map a grounded reason for its layout, cover, and objectives. The overall footprint is rectangular and mirror-symmetric along its central axis so neither team has an advantage — whatever shape, cover, and elevation appears on one half is reflected on the other. At each far end stands a team base: a sheltered staging compound with a protected spawn area, a forward exit balcony or gate feeding outward, and an objective point (a capture site or planting zone) just in front of it. Between the bases run the three lanes. The central lane is the widest and most exposed, a long open thoroughfare across a refinery yard with crates, low barriers, raised catwalks, and a contested central structure or courtyard at the midpoint that serves as the map's primary flashpoint. The two flanking side lanes are narrower and more enclosed — one threading through stacked shipping containers, pipework, and tight industrial alleys, the other winding through warehouse interiors and loading docks — offering close-quarters engagements and flanking opportunities. Lateral connector passages, doorways, and choke points link the three lanes at regular intervals so players can rotate sideways between routes, creating the interlocking flow typical of lane-based competitive maps. Verticality is layered throughout: scaffolding, gantries, ramps, rooftops, and ground-level cover give multiple sightline heights and peek angles. The structures are weathered industrial architecture — corrugated metal, concrete, steel framing, fuel tanks, machinery, and debris — unified by the abandoned-refinery theme, with destructible-looking clutter and tactical cover scattered to support both long-range duels in mid and tight skirmishes along the flanks.
Overall scene bounding box coordinates: origin (-30.00, 0.00, -40.00) m, dimensions (60.00, 22.00, 80.00) m

Each scene is always subdivided into a set of subregions. Each subregion can contain further subregions inside or the set of objects that forms it. The scene is composed as a tree with every object or region parented to another object or region. 

